data('FOUNDATIONS-SPIKES',9,'9–26; blue spike, rate, synapse, input signs, recurrent connectivity, tuning, population code, decoding and encoding','18–26: rate versus coordinate then vector over neurons','18: r_i=b_i+k_i theta, with rate and slope units;26 interprets the vector','18 negative-rate range;28 finite maps versus expected maps;35 no storage-location inference',39,'Reading guide7 neuron and27 place cell/hippocampus; calculus and vectors are assumed','Main Burak–Fiete2012 pp1–2 and main7–9 define spike-rate feedback and tuning. Eye2022 Methods2–7 include position, velocity, acceleration and threshold. Mainali2025 model and map methods distinguish expected field from finite extracted field. Saved2026CA3–CA1 source introduction explicitly gives different recurrence.','A shared value can be described by one cell or a population; angle and physical position are two represented variables, not competing circuits. Criteria: rate tuning and measurement uncertainty; scope: define the representation before dynamics.')
