data('FOUNDATIONS-ATTRACTOR',9,'9 state/fixed point;11 continuous attractor/manifold and neutral direction','15–41: invert rates to x,theta; add/subtract dynamics to get xdot=-ax and theta dot=0','43–48:5deg gives50,30; +3,+3 keeps5deg while+3,-3 gives6.5deg','21 positive rates;54 teaching geometry and nonperpendicular-projection limit',58,'Population rate vector at foundations20–26 precedes state geometry','Add and subtract the stated equations: xdot=(rdot1+rdot2)/2=-ax; theta dot=(rdot1-rdot2)/(2k)=0. With b40,k2, the given coordinates recompute exactly. Actual SVG labels, solid recovery and dashed imposed change agree. Burak–Fiete Fig1/SI7–18 support the general flow geometry.','Common and opposing perturbations begin at the same state; criteria: retained angle and deterministic return. They are two disturbance directions, not two mutually exclusive memory mechanisms.')
data('FOUNDATIONS-DIFFUSION',58,'74 Brownian mean-zero independent Gaussian increments and continuous paths;86 RMS','58–86: add independent increment variances;112–121 derive shared-history covariance','90–110: D=.02,v=.1;0.35s RMS=.118322deg=7.0993arcmin;cross4s, each displacement.4deg and squared contribution.16deg²','60–62 increment assumptions;74 approximation;86 equal-coordinate condition;123 boundaries and variableD',127,'Covariance and MSD split at foundations97–128; continuous family at persistence9–54','Variance addition gives2Dndt. Brownian increment variance gives2Dt and shared increments give2Dmin(s,t). For biased mean vt, MSD=v²t²+2Dt. Exact recomputation matches all values. SI30 p7 is normalized Gaussian with variance2Dt; ring squared distance is bounded by pi². The figure envelope is an RMS scale, not a trajectory boundary.','Random spreading and fixed bias use different mean and time laws; criteria: variance, RMS and MSD. The comparison keeps noise D fixed while adding mean velocity; finite/periodic domains are separately limited.')
